Q: How to use jest to test a function&#39;s return value(array)? A: <p>In the year 2023, <strong>Jest</strong> version-<code>&quot;jest&quot;: &quot;^29.5.0&quot;</code> you can use <code>toBeInstanceOf()</code> to check the type.</p>
<hr />
<p>If you want to check the return type of a function you can use the syntax below.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Just replace <code>yourFunc</code> with the proper name of your function</p>
</li>
<li><p>Replace <code>funcParams</code> with the parameters your function receives.</p>
<pre><code> import { describe, expect, test } from &quot;@jest/globals&quot;
  import { yourFunc } from &quot;../yourFunc&quot;

  describe(&quot;Test function - yourFunc&quot;, () =&gt; {
    test(&quot;expects that yourFunc returns an array type&quot;, () =&gt; {
      const returnValue = yourFunc(funcParams)
      expect(returnValue).toBeInstanceOf(Array)
    })
  })
</code></pre>
</li>
</ul>

Q: How can I align align text from top of a div? A: <p>This can be achieved using flexbox. Setting .langelis to <code>display: flex;</code> and using <code>align-items: center;</code> will have all child elements align themselves in the middle, vertically. Using flex also allows you to forgo floats and positions, as it will default to <code>flex-direction: row;</code> , stacking items left to right.</p>
<p>You can also use <code>inline-flex</code> depending on the context, if necessary.</p>
<p><em>Note: I cleaned up selectors for this so it will run in a snippet, you may need to make the more specific again depending on your needs. The clear div is also likely unnecessary since there are no floats anymore.</em></p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>#services {
  width: 1010px;
  height: auto;
  min-height: 320px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

#services .langelis {
    width: 510px;
    min-height: 140px;
    border: 1px #000 solid;

    display: flex;    
    align-items: center;
}

#services .langelis .icon {
  width: 65px;
  border: 1px #000 solid;
}

#services .langelis .txt {
  width: 440px;
  border: 1px #000 solid;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div id="services"&gt;
  &lt;div class="langelis"&gt;
    &lt;div class="icon"&gt;
      &lt;img src="images/knyg.jpg" alt="knyga" /&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class="txt"&gt;
      &lt;div class="sub"&gt;
        &lt;h1&gt;Lorem Ipsum&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;Lorem Ipsum is simply dummy text of the printing and typesetting industry. Lorem Ipsum has been the industry's standard dummy text ever since the 1500s..&lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;div class="clear"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Reload page after submit in iframe (javascript/jquery) A: <pre><code>$("#publish").click(function() {
    $('#inputs').ajaxSubmit({
        success:function(){
            //alert("Reload called");
            parent.location.reload();
        }
    });
 });
</code></pre>

<p>This worked.</p>
